      "writtenOn": "2025-01-29T17:18:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I would be careful with changing public API\n\nNothing is changing about the public api. GrPluginRestApi is what plugins interact with, none of those methods change.\n\n\u003e I also think it could be less complex if we use headers in implementation and not make more complex FetchOptionsInit interface. But that\u0027s nit.\n\nFetchOptionsInit has not been introduced in this CL. (Though the reason I added it before, is because constructing AuthRequestInit is cumbersome at the callsite).\n\nAs for requestOrigin, I didn\u0027t want it to be part of other headers, because it has special handling, so it looks clearer this way to me. \n\nI am not entirely sure tbh, what you mean by it looking less complex, I would still need to change all the same methods, except I would need to add headers argument instead of adding requestOrigin argument",
